    description: "WHAT (as reported)\naxum (the axum repository's examples/): 74 routes found in 44 of 55 example files, with handler names. Two gaps:\n1. A method chain on one path loses methods: in todos, .route(\"/todos\", get(todos_index).post(todos_create)) was missed while PATCH and DELETE on another path were found.\n2. key-value-store: nothing found, not even .route(\"/keys\", get(list_keys)).\n\nRelated, distinct: WI-basid (tower/hyper impl Service).\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # 07f4
